        <briefdescription>
<para>Constructs the <ref refid="classServer" kindref="compound">Server</ref> and transfers control to it. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>There is no command-line parsing: every setting is read from the environment by <ref refid="classConfigurator" kindref="compound">Configurator</ref> while the <ref refid="classServer" kindref="compound">Server</ref> is constructed. The unique_ptr owns the <ref refid="classServer" kindref="compound">Server</ref> for the whole process; because <ref refid="classServer_1a30362b937b125d27916cf595bfc4c1a7" kindref="member">Server::run()</ref> blocks until the event loops stop, the object survives long enough to finish its post-run shutdown sequence. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">argc</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Unused; retained only for the standard signature. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">argv</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Unused; retained only for the standard signature. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The status returned by <ref refid="classServer_1a30362b937b125d27916cf595bfc4c1a7" kindref="member">Server::run()</ref>, or EXIT_FAILURE if a std::exception escapes it. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Only std::exception is caught; an exception that does not derive from it would terminate the process. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classServer_1a30362b937b125d27916cf595bfc4c1a7" kindref="member">Server::run()</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
