    <briefdescription>
<para>Process entry point: build the <ref refid="classServer" kindref="compound">Server</ref> and translate uncaught exceptions into a failure exit status. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This file contains nothing but the program&apos;s <ref refid="main_8cpp_1a3c04138a5bfe5d72780bb7e82a18e627" kindref="member">main()</ref> function. It creates a single <ref refid="classServer" kindref="compound">Server</ref> object on the heap using a smart pointer, then hands control to <ref refid="classServer_1a30362b937b125d27916cf595bfc4c1a7" kindref="member">Server::run()</ref>. If anything throws a C++ exception during setup or shutdown, it prints a short reason to standard error and exits with a failure status.</para>
<para>WHY THIS FILE MATTERS IN THE SERVER: This is where the whole process begins. The operating system calls <ref refid="main_8cpp_1a3c04138a5bfe5d72780bb7e82a18e627" kindref="member">main()</ref> first; <ref refid="main_8cpp_1a3c04138a5bfe5d72780bb7e82a18e627" kindref="member">main()</ref> creates the <ref refid="classServer" kindref="compound">Server</ref>, and the <ref refid="classServer" kindref="compound">Server</ref> in turn configures and runs Drogon (the web framework) together with all the routes, filters and database helpers. Without this file there would be no starting point, so nothing would ever listen for HTTP requests. <ref refid="main_8cpp_1a3c04138a5bfe5d72780bb7e82a18e627" kindref="member">main()</ref> is also the last line of defence: it turns an uncaught exception into a readable error message and a non-zero exit code, which is what process supervisors and Docker expect when a program fails.</para>
<para>CONCEPTS TO LEARN (for beginners):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>RAII / smart pointers (std::unique_ptr): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/unique_ptr">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/unique_ptr</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Exceptions and try/catch: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/exceptions">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/exceptions</ulink></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Amr Osman <ulink url="mailto:dr3mro@gmail.com">dr3mro@gmail.com</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2026-11-16 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
